Restore the published ExORL Walker flip task expected by RLDP's benchmark.
Base: facebookresearch/offline_rl a53d64f5579e50ed6b93dff40e0bb6d1aea3b691
Source: https://github.com/denisyarats/exorl/blob/9cb4334fe730fd562ddccc5943d5d04884bf6350/custom_dmc_tasks/walker.py
Source license: Apache-2.0 (retained in walker.py).

The factory and flip reward are copied from ExORL. The flip flag is appended
so existing offline_rl positional arguments and spin behavior are preserved.
Angular momentum threshold/margin: 5; reward includes the standing factor.
The constructor's move_speed=8 is unused by the flip reward branch.
RLDP names ExORL but does not publish its original dmc_tasks dependency pin.
No published offline_rl commit defines flip; downgrading cannot restore it.

Apply from the project root after git submodule update --init --recursive:
  git -C third_party/offline_rl apply ../../scripts/walker-flip.patch

